<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        Two example deals, built in Python rather than written out here.

        A deal needs products, and this module ships none. Pointing an XML
        `ref` at a demo product would tie mart369_cart to whichever catalogue
        module happens to be installed, and break the load for a shop that
        brought its own. The method picks whatever is published, and does
        nothing at all if a deal already exists - so upgrading a shop that has
        set up its own never sprouts examples.

        Not noupdate: with it, the function only runs on a fresh install and
        a shop upgrading into this feature would never see the examples. The
        method guards itself instead - it does nothing when a deal already
        exists - so running on every upgrade is safe and seeds exactly once.
    -->
    <data>
        <function model="mart369.deal" name="_mart369_load_demo"/>
    </data>
</odoo>
